  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be defined as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable equalcolumns=\"true\" equalrows=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is continuous everywhere in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is the number of points where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is NOT differential then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mi>a</mi><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mi>c</mi></math> equals:</p>",
